course: dictionary
lesson: 11990
title: Chaise: an old carriage or a long chair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things, and the context tells you which one. «The old chaise rattled along the dusty road, pulled by one brown horse.» Rattled, dusty road and horse are the clues. A chaise here is a carriage, something people rode in long ago.
explain: «Grandma put her feet up on the chaise longue by the window.» Here the clue is put her feet up. A chaise longue is a long chair or sofa, with a back at one end, for resting your legs. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: In a story, a chaise tells you how people travelled. If you read about a chaise, you can guess they were going by horse, the old way, not by car or train.
fact: A chaise is a light carriage with two or four wheels, pulled by one horse.
fact: Many old chaises had a folding hood on top.
fact: A chaise longue is a long chair or sofa with a back at one end, where you can put your legs up.
fact: You will mostly meet a chaise in old stories and history books, or in the phrase chaise longue.
exercise: «The old chaise rattled along the dusty road, pulled by one brown horse.» What is a chaise in this sentence? | A tall tree by the road | *A light carriage pulled by one horse | A long chair for resting your legs | A kind of boat
exercise: «Grandma put her feet up on the chaise longue by the window.» What does chaise longue mean? | A small wooden box | *A long chair or sofa with a back at one end | A horse with a long mane | A window seat on a train
exercise: «The travellers climbed into the chaise, and the driver pulled the folding hood over their heads.» Find and copy the word that names the cover that folds. | chaise | *hood | travellers | driver
test: «Long ago, the doctor drove to the village in a chaise.» What does this sentence tell you about how the doctor travelled? | *By horse-drawn carriage | On foot | By train | By aeroplane
test: Ella says a chaise longue is a kind of carriage. Is she right? | *No, it is a long chair or sofa with a back at one end | No, it is a kind of bicycle | Yes, it is a carriage with four horses and a driver | Yes, it is a carriage with one horse
exam: «In the old history book, the chaise carried the family through the hills while the horse trotted on.» What does chaise mean here? | A kind of hat | A long sofa with a back | A cake | *A light carriage pulled by one horse
